  "lapsed_date": "03/07/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for soundproofing between lower floor flat and upper floor flat shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - The roof area of the extension hereby permitted ground floor extension shall not be used as a balcony, roof garden or similar amenity area without the grant of further specific permission from the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - No additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the sidewalls of the extensions hereby approved without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 7 - The application for the erection of a roof extension incorporating conversion of upper floors to create 2 self-contained flats and a single storey rear extension to shop, as shown on drawing numbers 0707/TP.01 & 0707/TP.02, received 23 March 2007; and 0707/TP.03C, received 17 May 2007; and 0707/TP.04E received 15 June 2007, is recommended for approval as the converted property is of an appropriate size and configuration for use as two units and its use as flats would not unduly harm the amenity of neighbours or adversely affect the character of the area. The proposed rear roof extensions and single storey rear extension would be compatible with the scale and form of the original building and would maintain the amenity of neighbouring properties and the character of the street scene. Therefore the proposed development complies with the relevant London Borough of Hounslow Unitary Development Plan 2003 policies; ENV-B.1.1 All New Development, H.3.4 Conversions of Houses to Flats, H.4.1 Housing Standards and Guidelines, H.6.4 Extensions and Alterations, T.1.4 Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities for Developments and the Supplementary Planning Guidance."
  ],
